    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000122543,
      "SummaryText": "The facility complies with applicable federal, state, and local laws. If an emergency were to occur, it is Nachurs Alpine Solutions' policy to notify Minnehaha County Emergency Management Department.  \n\nThe Nachurs Alpine Solutions Garretson facility stores 29.9% aqua ammonia in two (2) 30,000-gallon storage tanks. The maximum storage capacity of aqua ammonia in each tank is limited to 90% total capacity, or 27,000 gallons. In total, the maximum intended inventory of  29.9% aqua ammonia in the process is 54,000 gallons (401,760 lbs. assuming 7.44 lbs/gallon).\n\nThe facility complies with EPA's chemical accident prevention rule (40 CFR 68) and applicable state and local codes and regulations.  An accidental release of aqua ammonia resulting in death, injuries, significant property damage, sheltering in place, or causing environmental damage on-site or off-site has not occurred within the past five (5) years.\n\nIn the event of an emergency involving the covered process, it is the facility's policy to notify the Minnehaha County Emergency Management Department (LEPC) and request that they respond to the emergency.  The facility has determined that there are no planned changes to improve safety at this time. The last Hazard Review occurred on 7/15/2025 to review safety concerns and hazards at the facility."
    }
  ]
